2.1. No relicensing without consent. You may not sublicense, relicense,
     white-label, or represent any copy, fork, or derivative of this
     software as your own original work without the copyright holder's
     prior written consent. Forking on GitHub for personal noncommercial
     use under these same terms is permitted and does not require separate
     consent; publishing that fork as if it were an unrelated, independently
     authored project does.

2.2. No commercial use without consent. Any commercial use — including but
     not limited to selling, sublicensing, offering as a paid product or
     paid service (SaaS/hosting), bundling with a commercial product, or
     using within a for-profit business's internal operations — requires
     the copyright holder's prior written consent, regardless of what the
     PolyForm Noncommercial terms above might otherwise be read to allow.

2.3. No use as AI/ML training data. You may not use this software, or any
     portion of its source code, documentation, configuration, or other
     content, to train, fine-tune, distill, evaluate, or otherwise develop
     any machine learning or artificial intelligence model — including
     large language models, code-completion models, or any other
     AI system — whether for commercial or noncommercial purposes, without
     the copyright holder's prior written consent. This restriction applies
     regardless of whether the training is performed directly by you or by
     a third party on your behalf (e.g., submitting this code to a
     public/private model-training pipeline, dataset, or crawler).
     Automated tools whose *sole* function is to assist a human developer in
     reading, searching, or editing this exact repository during permitted
     personal/noncommercial use (e.g., an IDE's local code-completion index
     built only from this checkout) are not "training" for the purposes of
     this clause, but no output of such a tool may be used to build a
     redistributable model or dataset.

2.4. Requesting consent. To request written consent under 2.1, 2.2, or 2.3,
     open an issue at https://github.com/Ayazbog11/hermes-jarvis-all/issues
     or contact the copyright holder directly through their GitHub profile
     (https://github.com/Ayazbog11). Consent, if given, must be in writing
     (including email or a written GitHub comment/issue reply) to be valid.

2.5. Severability. If any part of Section 2 is found unenforceable in a
     given jurisdiction, the remaining parts of Section 2 and the PolyForm
     Noncommercial terms in Section 1 remain in effect.

